# -- conversions into CSSize ------------------------------------------------------

### Sign-extends `me` to `CSSize`. Every `S8` value fits, so this never fails.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
routine S8.to[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = sext[Me, CSSize](me)
    return r

### Sign-extends `me` to `CSSize`. Every `S16` value fits, so this never fails.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
routine S16.to[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = sext[Me, CSSize](me)
    return r

### Sign-extends `me` to `CSSize`. Every `S32` value fits, so this never fails.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
@target(size: 64)
routine S32.to[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = sext[Me, CSSize](me)
    return r

### Reinterprets `me` as `CSSize`. On this target the two types have the same width, so every value fits and the bits are unchanged.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
@target(size: 32)
routine S32.to[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = bitcast[Me, CSSize](me)
    return r

### Converts `me` to `CSSize`, always present on this target because every `S32` value fits.
### :returns: The value as an `CSSize`, wrapped in `Option`.
routine S32.to_checked[CSSize]() -> Maybe[CSSize]
    r: CSSize = me.to[CSSize]()
    return r

### Wrapping conversion to `CSSize`. On this target every `S32` value fits, so this equals `to[CSSize]` and nothing is wrapped or clamped.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
routine S32.to_wrap[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = me.to[CSSize]()
    return r

### Saturating conversion to `CSSize`. On this target every `S32` value fits, so this equals `to[CSSize]` and nothing is wrapped or clamped.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
routine S32.to_clamp[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = me.to[CSSize]()
    return r

### Reinterprets `me` as `CSSize`. On this target the two types have the same width, so every value fits and the bits are unchanged.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
@target(size: 64)
routine S64.to[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = bitcast[Me, CSSize](me)
    return r

### Converts `me` to `CSSize`.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
### :throws: Crashes with `IntegerOverflowError` when the value does not fit in `CSSize`.
@target(size: 32)
@track_caller
routine S64.to[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    if not (-2147483648 <= me <= 2147483647)
        crash_overflow()
    r: CSSize = trunc[Me, CSSize](me)
    return r

### Converts `me` to `CSSize`, always present on this target because every `S64` value fits.
### :returns: The value as an `CSSize`, wrapped in `Option`.
@target(size: 64)
routine S64.to_checked[CSSize]() -> Maybe[CSSize]
    r: CSSize = me.to[CSSize]()
    return r

### Converts `me` to `CSSize` when the value fits.
### :returns: The value as an `CSSize`.
### :absent: When `me` is outside the range of `CSSize`.
@target(size: 32)
routine S64.to_checked[CSSize]() -> Maybe[CSSize]
    fits: Bool = -2147483648 <= me <= 2147483647
    value: CSSize = trunc[Me, CSSize](me)
    r: Maybe[CSSize] = fits.then_present(value)
    return r

### Wrapping conversion to `CSSize`. On this target every `S64` value fits, so this equals `to[CSSize]` and nothing is wrapped or clamped.
### :returns: The same numeric value as an `CSSize`.
@target(size: 64)
routine S64.to_wrap[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = me.to[CSSize]()
    return r

### Converts `me` to `CSSize`, keeping the low 32 bits (modulo 2^32).
### :returns: `me` modulo 2^32, as an `CSSize`.
@target(size: 32)
routine S64.to_wrap[CSSize]() -> CSSize
    r: CSSize = trunc[Me, CSSize](me)
    return r

### Saturating conversion to `CSSize`. On this target every `S64` value fits, so this equals `to[CSSize]` and nothing is wrapped or clamped.
